  "id": "BIT-postgresql-2026-120145",
  "summary": "PostgreSQL logical replication can write to subscriber system catalogs, executing arbitrary code",
  "details": "Missing authorization in PostgreSQL logical replication allows a compromised publisher to execute arbitrary code as the operating system user running the superuser-owned subscription, via naming a system catalog as a replication target.  Only subscriptions owned by a superuser are vulnerable.  Versions before PostgreSQL 18.7, 17.12, 16.16, 15.20, and 14.25 are affected.",
